keywords:
  - Navier-Stokes
  - Beale-Kato-Majda
  - Kato local existence
  - Fujita-Kato
  - metriplectic
  - Frohmanian Symplectic Tether
  - Lean 4
abstract: >-
  Strictly conditional, expository companion repository. Theorem A
  (Beale–Kato–Majda continuation) is one-directional and conditional on
  Form B; Theorem B (Kato local existence) and Theorem C (Fujita–Kato
  small-data global regularity) are classical unconditional results, cited
  as such. The metriplectic tether B(F,G) is symmetric and degenerate,
  B(F,H) = 0. The Lean 4 file FrohmanianTripleArchitecture.lean checks the
  metriplectic algebra, degeneracy, alignment-kernel bound and Grönwall
  logic over abstract PDE input types, with zero sorry and only Lean's three
  standard axioms. Large-data global regularity (Clay Statement B) remains
  open; no Clay Millennium Problem proof is claimed.
